'''Miriwoong Sign Language''' is a developed [[Australian Aboriginal sign language]] used by the [[Miriwoong]], an [[Aboriginal Australians|Aboriginal]] community in the north of Australia. It is mostly used by the hearing community, but three deaf speakers have been identified. Speakers do not find [[Yolngu Sign Language]] to be understandable.<ref name=ISO>[http://www-01.sil.org/iso639-3/cr_files/2015-056.pdf ISO 639-3 Language Code Change Request Number 2015-056]</ref>

